\section{Per-Task CAR Breakdown}\label{sec:appendix_pertask_car}

Table~\ref{tab:per_task_car} decomposes CAR by task for all fine-tuned conditions, supporting the claim that per-task ordering is preserved across SDF loss weights (\S\ref{sec:avoidance_source}). Chocolate Pudding is consistently highest and BBQ Sauce consistently lowest across all conditions, including $\lambda = 0.1$. The intermediate tasks (Orange Juice and Milk) exchange rank between seeds but remain bounded by the extremes. This invariance indicates that avoidance patterns reflect the spatial statistics of collision-free demonstrations rather than geometric supervision.
